Quoting   <pendell@hotmail.com>:
>I left about a dozen orcish rogue corpses scattered around the dungeon.
> I used orcs for their infravision and their poison resistance. But
>even so they seemed to really stink when it came to hit points.
>I wondered if humans had some sort of advantage re: hit points.

Humans receive one more hit point initially, an average of half an extra
HP at low levels (up to 10 for rogues), and an extra HP per level
thereafter.

So they have an advantage, but not a very significant one. More important
is starting Con; you simply happened to start a rogue with a good
Constitution. That said, I don't think there's any class where the
orcish advantages are not outweighed by the advantages of some other
available race.

